# generated/ is the machine-written tier: every file under it is emitted by a
# script in this pack from sources tracked elsewhere in it, regenerated by
# assets/hooks/pre-commit whenever an input moves, and never hand-edited.
#
# Marking the whole tier — not one tree inside it — is what keeps that true in
# the places git and GitHub summarize a change. Without it, generated/seed-audit
# alone is 640 KB across 45 files, so a one-line fragment edit arrives as a
# 45-file diff that reads as hand-written work and buries the line somebody
# actually has to review. linguist-generated collapses it by default in pull
# requests and drops it from the repo's language statistics; -diff keeps it out
# of the textual diff, where the authoritative signal is the source commit
# beside it, not the render it produced.
generated/** linguist-generated
generated/** -diff
